      "created_at": "2025-09-10T04:21:36.041Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I have created a user (say ApiUser), and assigned a role to it with all permissions.<br>\nI also went to Role Permission manager and assigned permissions for a certain doctype.<br>\nI have also created an api_key and api_secret.</p>\n<p>But when i try to access the doctype with GET req in postman:<br>\n<a href=\"https://mywebsite/api/resource/Employee\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://mywebsite/api/resource/Employee</a>,<br>\nand in the header, i am passing “Authorization: token api_key:api_secret”, the doctype doesnt return any data. it gives a 200 success response but no data.</p>\n<p>And i can see a cookie getting set automatically in the cUrl after i send the req in POSTMAN.</p>\n<p>–header ‘Cookie: full_name=Guest; sid=Guest; system_user=no; user_id=Guest; user_image=’</p>\n<p>i dont understand why the cookie is getting set automatically if i am doing token based auth. I think because of that and the guest uid that it returns, i am not able to get the data.</p>\n<p>What should be done in this case?</p>",
